Message-ID: <041839806ef47d4eee74d47f720c577ba47011d8.1776946505.git.bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
In-Reply-To: <55d56a174a0f04520d4a1558630bb0b739074b13.1776946505.git.bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
References: <55d56a174a0f04520d4a1558630bb0b739074b13.1776946505.git.bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
From: Bertrand Marquis <bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Apr 2026 15:08:06 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH 21/28] virtio-msg: decouple bus limits from transport
 frame storage

This patch intentionally moves the core virtio-msg storage/protocol
envelope from 48 bytes to 128 bytes so bridge-capable transports have
enough headroom in the common message format.

Carry the bus-advertised max message size into core virtio-msg and enforce
it for request, response, and event traffic so oversized transfers fail in
the core transport path.

Keep AMP PCI at 64-byte FIFO slots while preserving safe zero-padding of
unused fixed-slot bytes, and advertise that smaller wire limit through
transport capabilities.

Signed-off-by: Bertrand Marquis <bertrand.marquis@arm.com>
---
